## Hard / risky work

Follow Master Workflow routing in `docs/CURSOR_DEVELOPMENT_OPERATING_SYSTEM.md`:

- Codex → complex implementation, difficult debugging, risky migration, hard/high-fidelity frontend
- Playwright / `browser-worker` → real browser E2E and UI evidence
- Cursor Explore → repository discovery
- Premium specialists (Fable/Sol/Sonnet/Gemini/Opus/Grok) only when their specialty is materially required
- Default premium usage = 0; no model fan-out on ordinary tasks

## Orchestration checklist

- Load only the minimum relevant context (`AGENTS.md`, constitution, smallest relevant spec when present).
- Inspect actual repository files, tooling, tests, and dirty worktree before changing implementation or tooling.
- Identify canonical owner / source of truth before adding state.
- Do not plan or implement while a material blocker remains.
- Preserve unrelated dirty worktree changes.
- Never request or expose secrets.
- A worker saying `DONE` is never completion proof — require evidence, verification, and false-completion audit for material claims.
- Parent remains accountable for handoffs, diff review, real checks, convergence, and final report.
